            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Court, the Supreme Court considered whether the statutory \u201csaving clause\u201d permits a federal prisoner to bypass the limitations of the Antiterrorism and Effective Death Penalty Act (AEDPA) when a motion under 28\u202fU.S.C.\u202f\u00a7\u202f2255 is \u201cinadequate or ineffective.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7fc24aa16225dbf8d0062f3010102176f90566c52d691205dba91358ab22b19d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7fc24aa16225-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 14,
              "start": 14
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "7fc24aa16225dbf8d0062f3010102176f90566c52d691205dba91358ab22b19d",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7fc24aa16225-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 17,
              "start": 17
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that the saving clause does not authorize such an end\u2011run around AEDPA, so the petitioner cannot bring his claim under 28\u202fU.S.C.\u202f\u00a7\u202f2241."
      }
    ],
